From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:29:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tests): allow Snake_case test names (CA1707) for
 tests/**; record owner test run

---
 .editorconfig                             | 4 ++++
 docs/development/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md | 8 ++++++--
 docs/development/SESSION_STATE.md         | 6 +++---
 3 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.editorconfig b/.editorconfig
index 898aff4..48775ab 100644
--- a/.editorconfig
+++ b/.editorconfig
@@ -32,3 +32,7 @@ dotnet_naming_style.underscore_camel.capitalization = camel_case
 dotnet_diagnostic.CA2007.severity = none
 # Localization is handled at the application layer (i18n), not via resx in every assembly
 dotnet_diagnostic.CA1303.severity = none
+
+[tests/**.cs]
+# Test method names use Snake_case sentences by convention
+dotnet_diagnostic.CA1707.severity = none
diff --git a/docs/development/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md b/docs/development/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md
index b0569c4..f353274 100644
--- a/docs/development/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md
+++ b/docs/development/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md
@@ -24,7 +24,11 @@ Last updated: 2026-11-09
 - `dotnet build src/DoubleUs.API` and `src/DoubleUs.Worker` (with all referenced libraries): 0 warnings, 0 errors, warnings-as-errors on.
 - Project reference rules checked with an ad hoc script against the real csproj files: all pass.
 
+## Owner-run result (2026-11-09, SDK 10.0.402, Windows)
+- Restore succeeded: the central package versions are valid on NuGet.
+- First `dotnet test` run failed on analyzer rule CA1707 (underscores in test method names). Fixed by scoping `CA1707` to `none` for `tests/**.cs` in `.editorconfig`. The fix is confirmed on a probe project in the authoring sandbox, but the **real test run after the fix is still pending**.
+- IntegrationTests has no tests yet by design; `dotnet test` prints a "no test is available" warning for it until Phase 1 task 3.
+
